11281 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Gangnam\047s \0428th School District\042 refers to the school catchment zone covering Gangnam and Seocho districts\054 historically associated with the highest\055performing public middle and high schools in South Korea\056 Access to this district became a powerful driver of residential demand\054 as Korean university admissions are determined almost entirely by a single standardized exam\054 making school environment and proximity to private tutoring academies \050hagwon\051 a high\055stakes consideration for families\056)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 11282 0 R
     /Pg 1805 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

11282 0 obj
  << /K [ 11281 0 R ]
     /P 11297 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1805 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

11283 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The reasons why an apartment that looks identical to one elsewhere in Seoul can command a price premium of billions of won in Gangnam are not simple\056 Nearly every factor that drives apartment prices \024 proximity to employment\054 school district quality\054 transportation\054 everyday amenities\054 green space\054 complex scale\054 and community facilities \024 converges in Gangnam at the highest level found anywhere in Korea\056 The districts of Gangnam and Seocho in particular host the country\047s largest concentration of businesses and workers\054 placing home and workplace within easy reach of each other\056 The cram school clusters centered around Daechi\055dong\054 Gangnam\047s unofficial tutoring hub\054 and the storied reputation of Gangnam\047s \0428th School District\042)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 11286 0 R
     /Pg 1805 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

