     /S /Link
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

11285 0 obj
  << /ActualText (\051 have made living in the area feel like a near\055prerequisite for education\055conscious Korean parents\056 On top of all this\054 Gangnam apartments have evolved into a proven inflation hedge \024 no longer simply a place to live\054 but a financial asset to hold\056\n\nThe cold statistics confirm it\056 Between 1995 and 2025\054 average apartment prices in Gangnam rose fifteenfold\054 while the first\055generation planned suburbs of the greater Seoul metro area \024 Pyeongchon\054 Jungdong\054 and Ilsan \024 managed only a sixfold gain over the same period\056ii The choice of which apartment to buy three decades ago has since produced staggeringly different outcomes in total household wealth\056 According to Statistics Korea\047s 2025 Household Finance and Welfare Survey\054iii the top ten percent of net\055worth holders now account for approximately 46 percent of all household net assets\056 The income Gini coefficient stands at around 0\056325\054 while the net\055asset Gini coefficient reaches 0\056625iv \024 a figure that reveals a society where the wealth gap dwarfs the income gap by a wide margin\056 In this environment\054 with mortgage regulations tightened further\054 the Gangnam apartment market has hardened into an exclusive arena accessible only to the rare few who can mobilize large sums of cash\056 The regulations designed to curb speculation have\054 ironically\054 become a protective fence around those who already own assets\056)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 11286 0 R
     /Pg 1805 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

