11313 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The difference between REITs \050Real Estate Investment Trusts\051 \024 the long\055dominant vehicle for indirect real estate investment \024 and the tokenization model is not simply a generational gap in technology\056 It is a clash of investment philosophies\056 A REIT pools capital from many investors\054 deploys it across a portfolio of properties\054 and distributes the returns as dividends\056v By bundling multiple buildings into a single basket\054 it spreads the risk of any individual asset across the entire investor base\056 REITs offer steady\054 predictable dividends \024 but investors have little visibility into which specific asset their capital is actually working in\056\n\nTokenization opens the door to something different\072 targeted investing in a single\054 named asset \024 a specific unit in a specific building\054 say\054 in Apgujeong\056 Security Tokens \050STs\051\054 which have been moving toward regulatory formalization through Korea\047s financial regulatory sandbox and the Financial Services Commission\047s 2023 framework for token security issuance and distribution\054vi allow investors to hold rights directly tied to the income stream of a particular asset\056 If REITs are like boarding an aircraft carrier \024 stable\054 collective\054 going wherever the fleet goes \024 tokenization is like each investor piloting their own boat to the exact spot they want to claim\056 One philosophy pursues safety through the dilution of risk\073 the other pursues returns through the deliberate selection of it\056 One treats the investor as a passenger\073 the other treats them as the navigator\056)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 11314 0 R
     /Pg 2273 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

