11332 0 obj
  << /ActualText (On the cost side\054 tokenization also removes the friction embedded in legacy systems\056 Blockchain\055based smart contracts automate income distribution and asset management\054 replacing the high fixed fees paid to fund managers and custodians with code\056 This dissolves a structural inefficiency that has long made it impractical to wrap a single apartment \024 too small\054 too specific \024 inside a REIT structure\056 That said\054 expecting tokenization to fully displace REITs anytime soon would be premature\056 Until the exchange infrastructure and settlement systems for security token markets are sufficiently mature\054 token markets will struggle to match the proven liquidity that REITs provide\056 Real estate STOs2\051 are better understood as a complementary instrument \024 one that absorbs the micro\055scale investment appetite REITs cannot serve \024 and will earn their place as a mainstream asset management tool only after establishing a stable regulatory footing\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 11333 0 R
     /Pg 2629 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

