11336 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Gangnam apartments have emerged as the natural frontier for tokenization not simply because they are expensive\056 It is their remarkable degree of standardization that makes them function as a genuine financial instrument\056\nThe 84\055square\055meter floor plan has become so deeply embedded in Korean property culture that it has acquired its own nickname\072 \042gugmin pyeonghyeong\042 \050the national unit\051\056 Koreans shorten this to \042gugpyeong\042 in everyday conversation\054 and a listing described simply as \0423 beds\054 2 baths\042 is understood by most Koreans to mean exactly 84 square meters \024 no further explanation needed\056 Prices are further stratified with precision according to developer brand\054 building age\054 and complex size\054 and this hierarchy is tracked in real time through the KB Price Index \024 Korea\047s authoritative benchmark for residential property valuation\056 Where American or European real estate generates enormous friction in valuation because every home has a different design and condition\054 Gangnam apartments have already been translated into clean\054 tradeable data\056\n\nThe second advantage is unrivaled liquidity\056 For asset tokenization to work in practice\054 investors need the confidence that they can exit at fair value whenever they choose\056 Gangnam apartments maintain the deepest pool of ready buyers even in times of crisis \024 a characteristic that closely resembles government bonds\056 Tokenizing an asset with thin demand is little more than manufacturing paper that nobody trades\056 Gangnam apartments\054 by contrast\054 represent a point of aspiration for the entire country\072 an asset whose value is universally understood and universally coveted\056 Tokenizing a Gangnam apartment\054 then\054 is not merely a real estate transaction\056 It is the act of placing an already\055financialized Korean safe haven asset onto a digital rail\056)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 11337 0 R
     /Pg 2629 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

