11391 0 obj
  << /ActualText (principal or interest in the interim\056 The buyer is freed from repayment pressure\073 the investors gain access to a prime asset\056 It is a structure designed for mutual benefit \024 though regulators may scrutinize it as a workaround for mortgage lending rules\056 To preempt this\054 the tokens must be clearly defined as performance\055based investment products with no guaranteed return and full exposure to capital loss \024 not fixed\055income instruments in disguise\056\n\nOne structural risk in this partnership model is bankruptcy remoteness\056 If Ms\056 B\047s other business ventures fail and she files for personal bankruptcy\054 what happens to the token holders\077 In a standard insolvency\054 the apartment would go to auction and the bank\054 as a senior secured creditor\054 would be first in line\056 Token holders could find themselves with nothing\056 This risk can be substantially mitigated through a trust structure\072 if Ms\056 B places the apartment in trust with a licensed trustee\054 and the trustee issues the tokens and manages investor relations\054 the asset becomes legally ring\055fenced \024 inaccessible to other creditors before the trust\047s obligations are settled\056\n\nThe risk of moral hazard \024 specifically\054 the concern that Ms\056 B might pocket sale proceeds without distributing the investors\047 share \024 is solved more elegantly still\056 A smart contract can be designed so that the moment sale proceeds are received\054 30 percent is automatically and instantly distributed to token holders\054 with no possibility of delay or diversion by the owner\056 Trust is no longer a matter of character\073 it is enforced by code\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
