11414 0 obj
  << /ActualText (A structural principle runs through all three scenarios\072 while anyone can technically issue tokens\054 deploying them as a financial instrument requires proper legal authorization\056 Article 11 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Actix prohibits unlicensed financial investment activities\054 and if token arrangements are treated as private money lending\054 the income tax rate on such earnings can reach 27\0565 percentx \024 a punishing outcome compared to the alternatives\056\n\nThe most efficient legal pathway is for the property owner to place the asset in trust with a licensed trustee\054 who then issues beneficial interest certificates backed by that asset\056 The Capital Markets Act explicitly permits licensed trustees to issue such certificates under monetary trust agreements\054xi and the scope of this framework has expanded through the Financial Innovation Support Actxii to cover non\055monetary trust assets including intellectual property\054 artwork\054 and real estate\056 Income earned by token holders under this structure is likely to be classified as dividend income\054 subject to a withholding tax rate of 14 percent \024 or 15\0564 percent including local income tax\056xiii Property tax and comprehensive real estate tax obligations for trust assets remain with the original owner\054 not the trustee\054xiv preserving the integrity of Korea\047s existing real estate tax system while opening the door to new investment structures\056\n\nThe tax advantage for investors is meaningful\056 A direct purchaser of real estate faces capital gains tax of up to 45 percent on disposal\056 A token investor\054 by contrast\054 holds a beneficial interest certificate \024 a financial instrument \024 issued by the trustee\054 and the returns on that instrument are likely to be taxed as dividend income at 15\0564 percent withholding\056 The legal foundation for this was significantly strengthened when amendments to the Electronic Securities Act and the Capital Markets Act passed the National Assembly in January 2026\054xv formally bringing token securities within the regulated capital markets framework\056 Tokens are no longer an experiment operating in a legal grey zone \024 they are a designable\054 institutional\055grade asset class\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 11415 0 R
     /Pg 4115 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

