  << /ActualText (The periodic redemption right carries an inherent danger\072 the house\055run\056 If every token holder simultaneously demands redemption \024 a scenario analogous to a bank run\054 but specific to this asset structure \024 the system breaks down the moment aggregate redemption requests exceed the owner\047s capacity to raise cash\056 An owner who has already deployed the capital raised through tokenization into living expenses or business ventures may find themselves facing personal bankruptcy and a wave of investor losses if large\055scale redemptions converge at once\056 Preventing this requires carefully engineered controls\072 annual redemption caps\054 market\055priority sale mechanisms that require investors to seek a buyer on the open market before triggering the owner\047s buyout obligation\054 and liquidity buffers\056 In short\054 tokenization is only sustainable if the system is designed to protect not just investors\054 but also the apartment owners who supply the market\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 11486 0 R
     /Pg 5291 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

