11489 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The most robust mitigation against house\055run risk is to bring a bank or major financial institution into the structure from the outset as a committed liquidity provider\056 Under this model\054 if a token holder cannot find a buyer on the secondary market\054 the financial institution steps in and purchases the token at a pre\055agreed floor price \024 typically a modest discount to market value\056 This transforms liquidity from a structural aspiration into an institutional guarantee\056\n\nIn this model\054 the financial institution\047s role extends well beyond capital provision\056 It acts as a trustee \024 monitoring asset value\054 overseeing dividend disbursements\054 and intervening if the owner falls behind on committed rent payments or distributions\056 If the owner defaults\054 the institution has the contractual authority to compel a sale and make token holders whole from the proceeds\056 This is\054 in essence\054 the model that transforms tokenization from a clever structure into a durable financial product\072 the presence of a credible institutional counterparty that can absorb liquidity shocks and enforce the rules when individual actors cannot or will not\056)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 11490 0 R
     /Pg 5291 0 R
