11504 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Jeonse is a uniquely Korean rental arrangement in which a tenant pays a large lump\055sum deposit \024 typically 50\02380\045 of the property\047s market value \024 directly to the landlord at the start of the lease\056 No monthly rent is paid\056 The landlord invests or uses the deposit during the tenancy and returns it in full when the lease ends\056 The system functioned as an informal credit market for decades before receiving formal legal recognition\056)
