11527 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The deeper question is the relationship between law\054 market\054 and state\056 Which came first \024 the state or the market \024 is an argument as old as the chicken and the egg\054 and just as unresolvable\056 What matters is not the sequence but the dynamic\072 state and market have grown together through cycles of thesis\054 antithesis\054 and synthesis\054 with law serving as the counterweight that maintains the balance between them\056 When law tilts too far toward the state\054 dense regulation strangles the market\056 When it tilts too far toward the market\054 those outside the law\047s protection become collateral damage\056 Law\047s proper role is to act as the calibrating force between these two poles \024 though finding that balance is never easy\054 given that those who write the law are rarely neutral between state power and market freedom\056 The regulatory debate around tokenization is playing out on exactly this tilted terrain\056 The question it poses is whether blocking tokenization represents balance\054 or whether bringing a new market inside the regulatory tent is the more balanced choice\056)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 11528 0 R
     /Pg 6005 0 R
     /S /Span
