11578 0 obj
  << /ActualText (As the pace of technological innovation accelerates\054 a new generation of scholars and entrepreneurs has stepped forward to make sense of what is happening\056 Professor Carlota Perez\054 who has spent her career studying the socioeconomic impact of technological change\054 argues that for the gains of a technological revolution to be fully realized\054 a corresponding reorganization of social and institutional structures is required \024 and that this process follows a recurring historical cycle\056xxii British journalist William Rees\055Mogg and American investor James Dale Davidson\054 in their co\055authored The Sovereign Individual\054 contend that the information revolution will erode state control and transfer greater autonomy and power to individuals\056xxiii Alex Karp\054 co\055founder and CEO of Palantir\054 argues in The Technological Republic \024 also co\055authored \024 that the technology industry should stop keeping the state at arm\047s length and instead rebuild its relationship with government\054 positioning itself at the center of national challenges rather than outside them\056xxiv And Balaji Srinivasan\054 former CTO of Coinbase and formerly a general partner at Andreessen Horowitz \050a16z\051\054 proposes in The Network State a new model of community built on blockchain and the internet \024 a successor form to the nation\055state\054 in           \052)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 11579 0 R
