11587 0 obj
  << /ActualText (which code and network infrastructure reorganize the existing order of sovereign nations\056xxv Taken together\054 what these arguments share is a single premise\072 technology has already emerged as a new form of power\054 and it is already driving the change\056\n\nTwo opposing forces are colliding over the speed and direction of this transition\056 On one side stands the camp of regulatory caution \024 the decelerationists\056 Centered on public authority and the established legal elite\054 this camp prioritizes order\054 stability\054 and due process\054 and instinctively applies existing legal standards to new technologies before entertaining the possibility of new frameworks\056 In the blockchain space\054 decelerationists want regulators to approach tokenization with caution\054 punitive tax treatment to remain in place\054 and any new financial product to pass through repeated rounds of legal opinion before it can proceed\056 In the AI space\054 they point to rising technological unemployment and the hacking risks of AI agents as grounds for slowing the pace of innovation\056\n\nOn the other side stands accelerationism\056 Centered on the technology elite\054 this camp leads with innovation and disruption\054 arguing that technology is already rewriting the terms on which law and state authority operate \024 and that existing legal frameworks and bureaucratic inertia are actively impeding progress\056 At the center of this camp stand figures like Alex Karp\054 Elon Musk\054 and Peter Thiel \024 co\055founder of PayPal and Palantir\054 founding partner of Founders Fund\054 and early investor in Facebook\054 LinkedIn\054 and a roster of transformative companies\056 These are individuals who combine world\055class capital with the conviction that technology should be pointed at changing the world\054 not accommodating it\056\n\nThe tech elite are already moving into spaces where state capacity has faltered or bureaucracy has calcified\054 quietly absorbing decision\055making authority that once belonged exclusively to governments\056 Elon Musk\047s SpaceX has provided Ukraine with Starlink satellite internet since the outbreak of the Russia\055Ukraine war in 2022\054 effectively controlling the communications infrastructure of an active conflict\056xxvi And in early 2026\054 Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei made headlines when he refused a request from the U\056S\056 Department of Defense \024 which sought access to Claude for what it described as \042lawful purposes\042 including autonomous weapons and mass surveillance \024 on the grounds that doing so would require compromising the AI\047s safety guardrails\056 The confrontation ended with Anthropic holding its position against the Pentagon\056xxvii Both episodes would have been almost unimaginable a decade ago\056 They are evidence that the influence of technology\055holding entities has grown to a point where it can stand level with state power\056\n\nPulling these threads together\072 history shows that markets precede law\054 and that the dialectic between them is how progress unfolds\056 New legislation arrives\054 but the energy of the market finds the gaps and builds new structures in the space between the rules\056 The structural limitations of Rule of Law systems are coming into sharper focus at the same moment that code\055based enforcement is emerging as a credible alternative\056 And the collision between the decelerationists and the accelerationists is not a temporary argument \024 it is a structural feature of the transition we are living through\056\n\nHow does any of this connect to Gangnam apartment tokenization\077 The connection compresses into a single question\072 when someone says \042the law       \052)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 11588 0 R
     /Pg 7149 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
