11603 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This report began with a single question\072 can Gangnam apartment tokenization actually work\077 To answer it\054 we walked the terrain of technology\054 cut through the thicket of law and taxation\054 and traced the historical currents running beneath both\056 The conclusion is simpler than the journey\072 yes \024 with constraints\056\n\nOn the technology side\054 the infrastructure is already largely in place\056 Trust\055based beneficial interest certificate structures\054 smart contract\055automated income distribution\054 bankruptcy remoteness mechanisms\054 and secondary market trading systems are all designable and executable today\056 The January 2026 amendments to the Electronic Securities Act and the Capital Markets Act have sharpened the legal foundation further\054 bringing the issuance and distribution of security tokens clearly within the regulated financial system\056\n\nWhat remains is the harder work of tax and policy refinement\056 The punitive acquisition tax surcharge on corporate purchasers\054 the unresolved ambiguities in how token securities are taxed\054 and the potential conflicts with the existing real estate tax regime are all problems the market cannot solve on its own \024 they require legislation and deliberate policy design\056 How quickly and precisely that work gets done will determine where Korea stands in the global race to establish tokenization as a mainstream financial infrastructure\056\n\nViewed from a wider angle\054 this is not simply a question of whether to permit one new financial product\056 Tokenization is part of a larger transformation \024 one that is redistributing the standards of rights\054 redesigning the enforcement pathways of trust\054 and ultimately rewiring the connective tissue of the global economic order\056 Korea has been here before\056 In the early 2000s\054 Cyworld\047s dotori \024 its virtual currency \024 was a prototype of digital money\056 The domestic court cases that wrestled with the trading and ownership of Lineage game items were among the earliest attempts anywhere to give digital assets legal standing\056 But those pioneering experiments never scaled into global standards\073 they remained enclosed within individual services and eventually disappeared when those services closed\056 The strategic will to push a technological prototype into an institutional standard was not there\056\n\nGangnam apartment tokenization is a second chance at that ambition\056 Korea holds a rare combination of advanced IT infrastructure\054 a highly engaged retail investor base\054 and a portfolio of internationally recognized\054 standardized residential assets\056 In an era where code designs the rules and networks organize the order\054 standards are no longer adopted after the fact \024 they are engineered in advance\056 Whoever lays the new rails of global finance by connecting the small pieces of tokenization will occupy the center of the next era\056 Gangnam apartment tokenization could be the first section of track\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 11604 0 R
     /Pg 7455 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

